<configuration xmlns="http://jgitver.github.io/maven/configuration/1.1.0"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://jgitver.github.io/maven/configuration/1.1.0 https://jgitver.github.io/maven/configuration/jgitver-configuration-v1_1_0.xsd">
  <strategy>MAVEN</strategy>
  <mavenLike>true</mavenLike>
  <useGitCommitId>false</useGitCommitId>
  <autoIncrementPatch>true</autoIncrementPatch>
  <!-- jgitver's default is `master` alone, and `master` IS this repository's default branch,
       so the default alone would have worked. `main` is listed as well, deliberately: it costs
       nothing and it keeps a build on a branch named `main` from coming out as
       X.Y.Z-main-SNAPSHOT. DO NOT DELETE IT thinking it is dead. It is a harmless extra, not a
       leftover. What must not be removed is `master`.

       A clean X.Y.Z requires HEAD to be exactly an annotated vX.Y.Z tag, and that is necessary
       but NOT sufficient. Two more conditions, both measured by driving jgitver 0.14.0's own API
       against the existing v2.0.0 tag rather than reasoned about:

       1. HEAD must be on a branch named in nonQualifierBranches, or detached. On any other
          branch, VersionStrategy.enhanceVersionWithBranch runs unconditionally and appends the
          branch name even to a release version. Tagging v2.1.0 on release/2.1.0-combined with a
          clean tree computes 2.1.0-release_2.1.0_combined, not 2.1.0. This is the whole reason
          `master` above is load bearing.
       2. The tree must be clean, and one untracked file is enough to spoil it. GitUtils.isDirty
          is jgit's Status.isClean(). Dirty at the tag, on a branch, computes X.Y.(Z+1)-SNAPSHOT.
          The `useDirty` setting does NOT govern this: it only controls whether the literal
          qualifier `dirty` is appended. The patch bump reads dirtiness separately, and is
          suppressed only when HEAD is detached, which is why a measurement taken in a detached
          scratch clone once made this look harmless.

       Keep every double hyphen out of this comment. XML forbids one inside a comment, jgitver
       reads this file before anything else, and the failure is total: `mvn` aborts with a
       ParseError, no module builds, and all four gates report "no reports" rather than naming
       the cause. It cost a full gate run once. -->
  <nonQualifierBranches>main,master</nonQualifierBranches>
</configuration>